  "conclusion": [
    "R110-A/R109 user instructions increase by median 3.111% at low connections and 3.089% at 64 held connections. All six paired increases at each scale exceed the observed same-ELF A/A range [-0.150%, +0.000%].",
    "Branches increase by about 1.22-1.23%. Branch-miss/cycle A/A variability is much larger; do not attribute a hardware-specific router cost to those medians.",
    "Compared with R103 the candidate has fewer user instructions, while the physical router has several CPU regressions. Instruction count alone does not establish total CPU or router performance.",
    "The R110-A main.rs patch adds a clients.get_mut before the original loop lookup. This is a concrete extra source operation; its causal contribution must be isolated by a single ablation before retaining any runtime change."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Six balanced permutations form one descriptive cycle, not six IID confirmation blocks.",
    "A/A uses low-connection R109 only; it is an observed spread, not a guaranteed noise bound at every condition.",
    "PMU is Oracle hardware and user mode; kernel costs, other microarchitecture behavior and physical router regressions remain outside this localization.",
